| S200 | mkinitcpio(8) — https://man.archlinux.org/man/mkinitcpio.8 | docs | A | The mkinitcpio hook API and execution order — install hooks, runtime hooks, post hooks, and the five runtime hook points — for the lane's mkinitcpio initramfs-hook frontier | ABOUT RUNTIME HOOKS; ABOUT INSTALL HOOKS (add_runscript); ABOUT POST HOOKS; FILES — mkinitcpio 42.2, man date 2026-10-01 | Runtime hooks run in the order defined in the HOOKS variable and cleanup hooks in reverse; run_earlyhook runs once the API mounts are up and the kernel command line parsed; run_hook runs after the early hooks and user modules are installed; run_latehook runs after root has been mounted; run_cleanuphook runs as late as possible; run_emergencyhook runs before the emergency shell launched on boot failure; add_runscript guarantees the runtime script name matches the hook name | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/initramfs-hook-api-r25.md |
