| S202 | On scripts and hooks (Arch Linux Dev Blog) — https://devblog.archlinux.page/2026/on-scripts-and-hooks/ | docs | A | The upstream pacman maintainers' own model of alpm-install-scriptlet(5) versus alpm-hooks(5), and the hook lifecycle relative to the providing package, for the lane's Arch packaging-and-hook-semantics frontier | The two systems (Hooks bullets); Transaction example (Upgrading the package); Notes for package maintainers (Documentation) — dated 2026-08-09, authors David Runge and Arne Christian Beer | A pre-transaction task is only available and run once the package providing it is installed; a post-transaction task is only available while its package is installed; on upgrade the old package version's pre-transaction hooks run first and the new version's post-transaction hooks last; upstream states it is missing a documented ordering system for alpm-hooks(5) | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/pacman-hook-timing-r25.md |
| S203 | Overlay Filesystem (Linux kernel documentation) — https://raw.githubusercontent.com/torvalds/linux/v7.2/Documentation/filesystems/overlayfs.rst | docs | A | The overlayfs upper/lower/workdir contract, copy-up, lower-directory rename semantics and the index/permission rules, for the lane's btrfs/overlayfs frontier and the untested snapshot-boot path | Directories; renaming directories; Non-directories; Permission model; Sharing and copying layers — kernel tag v7.2 | The workdir must be an empty directory on the same filesystem as upperdir; with redirect_dir disabled rename(2) on a lower or merged directory fails with EXDEV; reusing an upperdir or workdir already used by another overlay mount may fail with EBUSY; failure to verify the lower root origin makes the mount fail with ESTALE; upperdir and workdir may be omitted, in which case the overlay is read-only | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/overlayfs-mount-contract-r25.md |
