| S205 | errno(3) — https://man.archlinux.org/man/errno.3 | docs | A | The symbolic errno vocabulary and the rule that errno is meaningful only alongside a failed return value, for the lane's errno-based failure-attribution frontier | DESCRIPTION (errno); List of error names; NOTES — Linux man-pages 6.19, man date 2026-05-28 | errno is significant only when the return value of the call indicated an error, and a successful call may change errno; the numeric value behind each symbolic name varies across UNIX systems and even across Linux architectures, so only the names are portable; EACCES, EPERM, EXDEV, EROFS, ESTALE and EBUSY are six distinct failure classes, not one permission error | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/errno-name-discrimination-r25.md |
