| S214 | mount(2) — https://man.archlinux.org/man/mount.2 | docs | A | The mount(2) syscall contract and its errno vocabulary, for the overlay and snapshot-boot mount attempt that the lane's untested path depends on | DESCRIPTION; ERRORS (EACCES, EBUSY, EINVAL, ENODEV, EPERM, EROFS); Additional mount flags — Linux man-pages 6.19, man date 2026-02-11, package core/man-pages 6.19-1 | Mounting requires the CAP_SYS_ADMIN capability, and a caller without the required privileges gets EPERM; mounting a read-only filesystem without MS_RDONLY gives EACCES, but some filesystems return EROFS for the same condition, so EACCES and EROFS are not interchangeable readings; stacking a new mount on an existing mount point created with the same source and target gives EBUSY; an unconfigured filesystemtype gives ENODEV; MS_RDONLY, MS_BIND, MS_REMOUNT, MS_MOVE, MS_REC and the four propagation flags are the operation selectors; MS_RDONLY is settable per mount point since Linux 2.6.16 | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/mount-errno-contract-r26.md |
| S215 | alpm-package(7) — https://man.archlinux.org/man/alpm-package.7 | docs | A | The pacman-7 ALPM package-file anatomy — mandatory metadata, the optional install scriptlet, and the data files — for the lane's Arch packaging-and-hook-semantics frontier | DESCRIPTION; CONTENTS (Metadata, Scripts, Data); EXAMPLES; SEE ALSO — package extra/alpm-docs 0.13.0-1, upstream alpm.archlinux.page | An ALPM package file is an optionally compressed tar archive containing mandatory metadata files plus optional scripts and data files; .BUILDINFO, .MTREE and .PKGINFO must be present at the root of every package; an alpm-install-scriptlet named .INSTALL may be present at the root; all data files are extracted to the root directory of the target system upon installation; by default all files and directories should be owned by root, and package files should never be placed in directories that contain user data | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/alpm-package-anatomy-r26.md |
