| S217 | PKGBUILD(5) — https://man.archlinux.org/man/PKGBUILD.5 | docs | A | The PKGBUILD build-description format and, critically, the install-scriptlet lifecycle, for the lane's Arch packaging-and-hook-semantics frontier | OPTIONS AND DIRECTIVES (pkgname, epoch, install, changelog, backup, source); PACKAGING FUNCTIONS; INSTALL/UPGRADE/REMOVE SCRIPTING — Pacman 7.1.0, man date 2026-10-15, core/pacman 7.1.0.r9.g54d9411-3 | The mandatory fields for a minimally functional PKGBUILD are pkgname, pkgver, pkgrel and arch; epoch forces a package to be seen as newer than any previous version with a lower epoch even where the version number would not trigger an upgrade; the install directive names a special install script copied into the package by makepkg, and the backup array names files that are saved when the package is removed or upgraded; the packaging functions are package, verify, prepare, build and check, run inside srcdir except package which runs inside pkgdir under fakeroot; and during an upgrade operation none of the install or remove functions will be called, while pre_install and post_install take the new package full version string, pre_upgrade and post_upgrade take the new then the old, and pre_remove and post_remove take the old | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/alpm-package-anatomy-r26.md |
| S218 | Linux 中文件系统的概述（SLES 15 SP7 存储管理指南 第 1 章） — https://documentation.suse.com/zh-cn/sles/15-SP7/html/SLES-all/cha-filesystems.html | docs | B | Chinese-language vendor documentation of the Btrfs subvolume layout, the rollback precondition, and the disk-space failure mode, for the lane's btrfs/overlayfs and errno-attribution frontiers and the East-Asian coverage gap | 1.2.2 SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 上的根文件系统设置（警告：回滚支持）; 1.15 文件系统查错; 1.15.1 Btrfs 错误：设备上没有剩余空间; 1.15.1.1 Snapper 快照使用的磁盘空间; 1.15.1.2 log、crash 和 cache 文件使用的磁盘空间 — publisher SUSE, inLanguage zh-CN, dcterms.created 2025-06-17, datePublished 2026-10-01 | 仅当您未移除任何预先配置的子卷时，SUSE 才支持回滚; the default root layout excludes /boot/grub2 architecture directories, /home, /opt, /srv, /tmp, /usr/local and /var from snapshots, each for a stated reason; a No space left on device error on the Btrfs root is usually caused by too much data held as snapshots; deleting snapshots does not delete them immediately and may therefore not free the space you need, so the documented procedure is btrfs filesystem show, btrfs fi balance start -dusage=5, snapper -c root list and snapper -c root delete, deleting the oldest snapshots first; the /var/log, /var/crash and /var/cache subvolumes can consume all available space during normal operation, which is what Btrfs subvolume quota support exists to prevent | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/btrfs-filesystem-troubleshooting-bilingual-r26.md |
| S219 | Linux ファイルシステムの概要（SLES 15 SP7 ストレージ管理ガイド 第 1 章） — https://documentation.suse.com/ja-jp/sles/15-SP7/html/SLES-all/cha-filesystems.html | docs | B | Japanese-language vendor documentation of the same Btrfs subvolume layout, rollback precondition and disk-space failure mode — the matched Japanese sibling of S218 — for the lane's btrfs/overlayfs and errno-attribution frontiers and the East-Asian coverage gap | 1.2.2 SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 上のルートファイルシステム設定; 1.15 ファイルシステムのトラブルシューティング; 1.15.1 Btrfsエラー: デバイスに空き領域がない; 1.15.1.1 Snapperスナップショットによるディスク容量の使用 — publisher SUSE, inLanguage ja, dcterms.created 2025-06-17, datePublished 2026-10-01 | The Japanese edition states the same rollback precondition as S218 and the same No space left on device failure mode, with the same four-step procedure of btrfs filesystem show, btrfs fi balance start -dusage=5, snapper -c root list and snapper -c root delete, and the same statement that deleting a snapshot does not immediately release the space; the Japanese edition is a first-party human localisation, not a machine translation, and the two chapters share a publisher, a creation date and a publication date | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/btrfs-filesystem-troubleshooting-bilingual-r26.md |
| S220 | Btrfs filesystem ioctl handlers (Linux kernel source) — https://raw.githubusercontent.com/torvalds/linux/v7.2/fs/btrfs/ioctl.c | code | A | The kernel's own errno returns for subvolume creation and snapshotting, and the BTRFS_IOC command surface, for the lane's errno-based failure-attribution frontier | __btrfs_ioctl_snap_create; create_snapshot; btrfs_ioctl_subvol_sync; btrfs_ioctl_fitrim; long btrfs_ioctl — kernel tag v7.2 | A snapshot source on a different filesystem returns EXDEV, with the kernel logging Snapshot src from another FS; a snapshot of a subvolume the caller does not own returns EPERM, with the kernel noting that subvolume creation is not restricted but snapshots are limited to own subvolumes only; a name containing a slash returns EINVAL and a name of . or .. returns EEXIST; snapshotting a root with no references returns ENOENT and a root that is not shareable returns EINVAL; snapshotting a subvolume with an active swapfile returns ETXTBSY and extent-tree-v2 filesystems return EOPNOTSUPP because snapshotting is not supported there; the ioctls that change the filesystem require CAP_SYS_ADMIN and return EPERM without it; and BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_SYNC distinguishes ENOENT for a subvolume that does not exist from EEXIST for one that is not deleted at all | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/mount-errno-contract-r26.md |
| S221 | mkinitcpio >= 42 更新在基于TPM2解锁LUKS的设备上可能需要手动干预（Arch Linux 中文社区） — https://www.archlinuxcn.org/mkinitcpio-42-requires-manual-intervention-for-tpm2-based-unlocking-of-luks-devices/ | docs | B | The Chinese-language community rendering of the mkinitcpio-42 TPM2 manual-intervention notice, for the lane's mkinitcpio-42 upgrade gate and its zero-Chinese-source gap | 文章正文（正文首段起） — published 2026 年 9 月 22 日, WordPress post id 1208, canonical self-link | From package version 42-1 the mkinitcpio systemd hook also includes the systemd-pcrosseparator.service service, per the systemd v261 plan; this affects the measurement of PCR values 0-7, 9 and 12-14; if the systemd hook is configured and the LUKS unlock depends on those values, the TPM2 in use must be re-enrolled; the guidance points to systemd-cryptenroll(1) and the ArchWiki systemd-cryptenroll article for fixed values, and to systemd-pcrlock(8) where a custom policy is relied on with systemd-pcrlock-make-policy.service disabled | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/mkinitcpio-42-upgrade-gate-cjk-r26.md |
| S222 | mkinitcpio — Arch Linux 中文维基 — https://wiki.archlinuxcn.org/wiki/Mkinitcpio | docs | B | The Chinese-language community rendering of the mkinitcpio hook doctrine — build, runtime and post hooks, the systemd-hook root-account disable, the emergency-shell parameter and the fallback image — for the lane's mkinitcpio frontier and its zero-Chinese-source gap | §3.3 钩子（HOOKS）（3.3.1 构建时钩子 / 3.3.2 运行时钩子 / 3.3.3 映像后处理钩子 / 3.3.4 常用钩子）; §疑难解答 → 无法访问控制台，root 用户被锁定; §标准急救过程 → 在一台机器引导成功，但在另一台引导失败; §生成 fallback initramfs 映像 — MediaWiki revision 35238, page last edited 2026 年 6 月 20 日 10:23 | The Chinese page divides hooks into 构建时钩子, 运行时钩子 and 映像后处理钩子 with a 常用钩子 list; it states that the systemd hook disables the root user and that enabling the emergency shell requires temporarily adding SYSTEMD_SULOGIN_FORCE=1 to the kernel parameters, linking the upstream systemd packaging commit that made the change; it documents the cross-machine failure mode as the autodetect hook filtering modules against the wrong hardware and the remedy as selecting the fallback image, then rebuilding on the new machine, then chrooting from a live medium; and it warns that the absence of a fallback initramfs removes the operator's second way in when the default image fails, so a bootable installation medium should be kept on hand | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/initramfs-hook-api-zh-r27.md |
| S223 | Linux btrfs uapi header (include/uapi/linux/btrfs.h) — https://raw.githubusercontent.com/torvalds/linux/v7.2/include/uapi/linux/btrfs.h | code | A | The BTRFS_IOC command surface and the subvolume creation and deletion flag semantics, for the lane's errno-attribution frontier and the snapshot-boot path | BTRFS_SUBVOL_RDONLY; BTRFS_SUBVOL_CREATE_ARGS_MASK; BTRFS_SUBVOL_DELETE_ARGS_MASK; BTRFS_SUBVOL_SPEC_BY_ID; struct btrfs_ioctl_get_subvol_info_args (parent_uuid); the BTRFS_IOC_* definition block — kernel tag v7.2 | The ioctl magic is 0x94 and the ioctl numbers are fixed by that magic, so the command surface is stable and enumerable: BTRFS_IOC_SNAP_CREATE is 1, BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_CREATE is 14, BTRFS_IOC_SNAP_DESTROY is 15, BTRFS_IOC_SNAP_CREATE_V2 is 23, BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_CREATE_V2 is 24, BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_GETFLAGS is 25, BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_SETFLAGS is 26, BTRFS_IOC_SNAP_DESTROY_V2 is 63 and BTRFS_IOC_GET_SUBVOL_INFO is 60; a read-only snapshot is requested with the BTRFS_SUBVOL_RDONLY flag, and BTRFS_SUBVOL_CREATE_ARGS_MASK admits only BTRFS_SUBVOL_RDONLY and BTRFS_SUBVOL_QGROUP_INHERIT, so a create or snapshot ioctl carrying any other bit is rejected; deletion carries a different mask, BTRFS_SUBVOL_DELETE_ARGS_MASK, admitting only BTRFS_SUBVOL_SPEC_BY_ID; BTRFS_SUBVOL_CREATE_ASYNC is marked deprecated since 5.7; the get-subvol-info structure returns the UUID of the subvolume the queried subvolume is a snapshot of, all zero for a non-snapshot subvolume, which is the machine-readable parent link; and BTRFS_FEATURE_INCOMPAT_EXTENT_TREE_V2 is the feature bit that round 2's EOPNOTSUPP return corresponds to | mined | 2026-10-23 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/btrfs-ioctl-surface-r27.md |
| S224 | 翻译团队（页面维护列表） — Arch Linux 中文维基 — https://wiki.archlinuxcn.org/wiki/Project:%E7%BF%BB%E8%AF%91%E5%9B%A2%E9%98%9F | docs | B | The Chinese community's own per-page translation-status ledger — 过期 / 未翻译 / 完成, with maintainer and notes — for measuring which parts of the Arch doctrine the Chinese community received and how current each rendering is | §2 页面维护列表; §翻译状态说明 (过期 / 未翻译 / 完成); the note 请按照拉丁字母顺序添加页面 — MediaWiki revision 35351, last edited 2026 年 7 月 19 日 07:42 | The ledger defines three translation states — 过期 for a page whose content is not synchronised with the English page, 未翻译 for a page that still contains English, and 完成 for a page synchronised with the English page — and then lists every claimed page with its state, its maintainer and a maintenance note; among the visible entries, Plymouth is 完成 and 长期维护中 under Amao.Run, GRUB is 完成 under Reverier, Kernel module is 完成 under Archeb, Trusted Platform Module is 完成 under Corna, Fstab and Fsck are 完成 under their listed maintainers, while Qt is 过期, Systemd-nspawn and Linux_Containers are 部分翻译, and ZFS, Nftables, Rust, Vim-adjacent entries and the packaging-guidelines page are in translation | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/translation-status-ledger-r27.md |
