| S228 | PKGBUILD — Arch Linux 中文维基 — https://wiki.archlinuxcn.org/wiki/PKGBUILD | docs | B | The Chinese-language community rendering of the Arch packaging semantics — the PKGBUILD variables and the complete .install scriptlet function table — for the lane's Arch packaging-and-hook-semantics frontier, which had no East-Asian channel until this row | §6.1 backup; §6.3 install; §6.4 changelog; §source; §noextract; §validpgpkeys; §完整性检验 — MediaWiki revision 34277, page last edited 2025 年 8 月 23 日 17:28, content language zh | The Chinese page gives the full .install scriptlet table in Chinese: pre_install and post_install each take one argument, the new version number; pre_upgrade and post_upgrade each take two, the new version number then the old version number; pre_remove and post_remove each take one, the old version number; every function runs chrooted into the pacman installation directory; the script must not end with exit or the remaining functions in it will not run; it points at /usr/share/pacman/proto.install as the template and notes that pacman hooks offer similar functionality; it records that makepkg recognises the .install file automatically and that it should not be listed in source; and it states the integrity-check strength order b2 > sha512 > sha384 > sha256 > sha224 > sha1 > md5 > ck | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/pkgbuild-semantics-zh-r27.md |
| S229 | 日本語訳 — The Linux Kernel documentation — https://docs.kernel.org/next/translations/ja_JP/index.html | docs | B | The scope of the official Japanese kernel-documentation translation itself — which documents the Japanese kernel community received — for the lane's East-Asian coverage question | the 日本語訳 toctree, which lists exactly four translated documents; the language-selection list, which names 中文翻译, 繁體中文翻譯, La documentazione del kernel Linux, 日本語訳, 한국어 번역, Documentação do Kernel Linux em Português and Traducción al español — kernel documentation tree next-20261023 | The Japanese translation of the Linux kernel documentation is complete in scope and narrow in coverage: it translates **four** documents and no others — 免責条項 (Disclaimer) 抄訳, process/howto, process/submitting-patches and process/submit-checklist — so every document it carries belongs to the kernel *development process*, and it carries **no** filesystem documentation at all; that is why there is no Japanese rendering of the overlayfs or btrfs documents, and the absence is a property of the translation effort rather than a failed fetch; the same index also names the Chinese (zh_CN and zh_TW), Italian, Korean, Portuguese and Spanish translations, so the Chinese kernel-documentation translation is a distinct channel with its own coverage to be measured | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/translation-status-ledger-r27.md |
| S230 | Snapper `/.snapshots` EACCES mechanism and limits — corpus/knowledge/snapper-eacces-mechanism.md | own-work | A | The lane's own re-runnable falsifier and mechanism statement for the standing `errno:13` observation, for the lane's errno-attribution frontier | § Current host evidence; § Rejected readings (R6); § Falsifier; § QUALITY check — the lane's own entry, verified-at 2026-10-19 | The lane's own entry holds the measurements the errno question rests on: `/` is `555 root:root` with no write bit and no ACL granting one; the local limine-snapper-sync.service declares `User=root` and `CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_SYS_ADMIN` and nothing else; the journal query matched **8** `errno:13` messages between 2026-10-16 and 2026-10-19; `snapper list-configs` prints no rows and `/.snapshots` does not exist; and `pacman -Qo /` reports no owning package with **0** root-directory entries in the filesystem mtree, which is why `pacman -Qkk` cannot report drift for the root-directory mode; its `[inf]` mechanism is that the unit lacks the CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE bypass needed to create `/.snapshots`, consistent with the observed EACCES but explicitly not a syscall trace; and its operator-only falsifier is `sudo systemd-run --wait --pipe -p CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_SYS_ADMIN test -w /` predicting `rc=1` against `sudo test -w /` predicting `rc=0` | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/errno-falsifier-amend-2026-10-23.md |
| S231 | mkinitcpio v42 `/sysroot` transition and recovery points — corpus/knowledge/initramfs-v42-sysroot-recovery.md | own-work | A | The lane's own record of the v42 `/new_root` to `/sysroot` transition and of the untested btrfs-overlayfs snapshot-boot path, for the lane's mkinitcpio and snapshot-boot frontiers | § Current host and compatibility surface; § Recovery entry points by stage; § Rejected readings (R5); § Falsifier — the lane's own entry, verified-at 2026-10-19 | The lane's own entry holds the compatibility surface the snapshot-boot question depends on: the configured HOOKS drop-ins omit `systemd` and name `plymouth`, `encrypt` and `btrfs-overlayfs`, so the busybox flavour applies; **2** configured runtime hooks hardcode `/new_root`; the v42 `init` contains **0** `/new_root` references against **7** in v41, with v42 mounting root on `/sysroot` and switching root there; and the predicted failure is specific — after a rebuild pairing v42 init with the unchanged `btrfs-overlayfs` hook, `run_latehook` checks `/new_root`, `findmnt --mountpoint` fails, and `\|\| return 0` exits successfully, so the overlay setup is a **silent no-op** rather than a visible failure; the entry also records that the mkinitcpio-42 TPM2 news is N/A to this configuration because the systemd hook is absent | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/snapshot-boot-preconditions-amend-2026-10-23.md |
| S232 | PKGBUILD — ArchWiki（日本語版） — https://wiki.archlinux.jp/index.php/PKGBUILD | docs | B | The Japanese-language community rendering of the Arch packaging semantics, and the only East-Asian source found for the .pacnew and .pacsave surface, for the lane's packaging-and-hook-semantics and drift frontiers | §6.1 backup; §6.3 install; §6.4 changelog; §整合性 — MediaWiki revision 40193, page last updated 2025 年 4 月 20 日 00:46, content language ja | The Japanese page gives the complete .install scriptlet table in Japanese: pre_install and post_install each run before and after extraction and take one argument, the new package version; pre_upgrade and post_upgrade take two, the new package version then the old; pre_remove and post_remove take one, the old version; every function runs chrooted into the pacman installation directory; and the script must not call exit or the remaining functions in it will not run; the `backup` section states the drift semantics the lane's .pacnew/.pacsave surface depends on — a new version is saved as file.pacnew rather than overwriting a file the user has modified, and on removal the modified file is left as file.pacsave unless the package is removed with `pacman -Rn` — and that the backup paths must be relative rather than absolute | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/pkgbuild-semantics-zh-r27.md |
| S233 | 中文翻译 — The Linux Kernel documentation — https://docs.kernel.org/next/translations/zh_CN/index.html | docs | B | The scope of the official Chinese kernel-documentation translation — which kernel-document sections the Chinese community received and which it declared outstanding — for the lane's East-Asian coverage question | the 中文翻译 toctree, covering how-to, the development-process documents, the internal-API manuals, the development tools, the user-oriented documents, the firmware documents, the architecture documents, the uncategorised documents and the glossary; and its three explicit TODOList entries — kernel documentation tree next-20261023 | The Chinese kernel-documentation translation is far broader than the Japanese one and it declares its own gaps: it covers the translation guide, the whole development-process set, the internal-API manuals (核心API文档, Linux驱动实现者的API指南, 内核子系统文档, 内核中的锁), the development tools and test guide, the **user-oriented documents** (Linux 内核用户和管理员指南, Linux 内核用户空间API指南, 内核构建系统), the firmware documents (Open Firmware 和 Devicetree), the architecture documents (MIPS, ARM64, RISC-V, OpenRISC, PA-RISC, LoongArch), the uncategorised documents and the glossary; and it lists three sections still outstanding in an explicit TODOList — trace/index, fault-injection/index and livepatch/index — with userspace tools and firmware-guide/index also marked as TODO; the tree exposes **no filesystems section**, so the filesystem layer — overlayfs, btrfs — is outside the Chinese translation as well as the Japanese one | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/translation-status-ledger-r27.md |
| S234 | Plymouth（源文） — Arch Linux 中文维基 — https://wiki.archlinuxcn.org/wzh/index.php?title=Plymouth&action=raw | docs | B | The per-page upstream revision and translation date behind the Chinese rendering of the Plymouth page, and the initramfs hook-ordering rule it states, for the lane's plymouth frontier and its translation-provenance question | the first line of the wikitext, `{{翻译状态\|Plymouth\|2024-08-30\|815520}}`; the `{{相关文章开始}}` / `{{Related\|静默启动}}` block; §mkinitcpio; §放慢启动速度以显示完整的动画; §使用 SimpleDRM — MediaWiki action=raw of the Chinese Plymouth page | The raw wikitext carries the translation-status template invocation, which states the upstream revision the translation was made from and the date it was made — the per-page drift measure that the rendered page hides behind a collapsed template; it also carries the initramfs hook-ordering rule, that if the systemd hook is used it must come before the plymouth hook and that on a dm-crypt-encrypted system the plymouth hook must come before the crypt hook; and it carries the operational facts that the boot log goes to /var/log/boot.log by default, that changing the theme requires the initrd to be rebuilt, and that on legacy UEFI the full-disk-encryption password prompt may fail to display with SimpleDRM, which plymouth.use-simpledrm=0 disables | mined | 2026-10-23 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/translation-provenance-r28.md |
